           (Runtime/getRuntime)\n            (Thread. ^Runnable (fn []\n                                 (request-stop! state w)\n                                 (.join poller ^long stop-join-millis))))\n          (.join poller))\n    ```\n    The only place `stop-join-millis` is used in headless mode is within the JVM shutdown hook thread to bound hook execution during external SIGTERM/SIGINT signals. The change at line 1349 does not alter the headless path.\n  - **Served mode (`--port`) \u0026 DHT-attached mode**:\n    When the poller encounters `(quit)`, `(:running? state')` evaluates to false, routing into `(drain! state' server' w)` (`main.cljc:1277`).\n    In `drain!` (`main.cljc:1227-1241`), the shutdown loop is strictly bounded:\n    ```clojure\n    (loop [state (update state :repl repl.dht/stop!)\n           server (some-\u003e server serve/stop!)\n           remaining stop-ticks]\n      ...\n      (cond\n        (shutdown-drained? state' server') state'\n        (zero? remaining) (do (println stop-timeout-text) state')\n        :else (do (wake/sleep! w tick-millis)\n                  (recur state' server' (dec remaining)))))\n    ```\n    `stop-ticks` (set to `200` at line 1095) guarantees that even if a server socket or DHT storage refuses to close or wedge, `drain!` terminates after 200 ticks (~20s), prints `stop-timeout-text`, closes index stores, and calls `exit!` (`.halt 0`).\n\n- **Can the Poller Run Forever?**:\n  - While running user code queued *before* `(quit)`: If a user submission loops infinitely, the poller thread executes it indefinitely. This is standard CLI / REPL behavior across modern runtimes (e.g. `python`, `node`, `clojure`), where closing `stdin` signals EOF on the input stream without prematurely killing running tasks.\n  - Once `(quit)` is reached: The shutdown drain is bounded by `stop-ticks` (200 ticks); it cannot spin or run forever.\n  - Interactive typed `(quit)`: As documented in lines 1340–1343, when `(quit)` is typed interactively while `stdin` remains open, `poll-loop!` completes `drain!` and calls `exit!` (`.halt 0`) directly, terminating the JVM before the main thread ever returns from `read-loop!`.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Adversarial Review of the Regression Test (`dht_process_test.clj:1202-1233`)\n\n- **Reproduction of the Owner's Shape**:\n  - The test sets up the exact sequence:\n    1. `\"(lang :yang.python/antlr)\"`\n    2. `\"even_squares = [x**2 for x in range(1, 11) if x % 2 == 0]\"`\n    3. `\"print(even_squares)\"`\n  - In Python, variable assignment is a statement that does not return a value. Appending `\"print(even_squares)\"` gives the test a deterministic stdout signal without altering the underlying comprehension compilation or execution path.\n- **Assertion and Regex Correctness**:\n  - The assertion `(is (some #(re-find #\"\\[4, 16, 36, 64, 100\\]\" %) (:lines bug)))` escapes brackets (`\\[...\\]`). It verifies the exact formatted sequence `[4, 16, 36, 64, 100]`. It cannot falsely match on whitespace or arbitrary digits.\n- **Hang Detection**:\n  - `run-submissions` sets a timeout of 90,000 ms (90s).\n  - If the linker spin or an undischarged occurrence cycle recurs, `process.waitFor(90000)` times out, `done` is false, the process is terminated, and `(is (:exited bug))` fails.\n  - If the process terminates prematurely without evaluating the queued lines, the output regex assertion fails.\n- **Execution Verification**:\n  - Ran `clj -M:test -i :slow -v yin.repl.dht-process-test/prompt-returns-after-filtered-comprehension-assignment-test`.\n  - Result: 1 test, 4 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Scope Discipline \u0026 Verification\n\n- **Diff Scope**: Strictly limited to `src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc` (removing the bounded join in favor of `(.join poller)`) and `test/yin/repl/dht_process_test.clj` (adding the regression test and runner helper). No extraneous modifications.\n- **Linter**: `clj -M:kondo --lint src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc test/yin/repl/dht